// Exception agent eval corpus. One case per line.
//
// Expectations are floors, not scripts. `acceptable_kinds` lists every answer
// a competent operator might defend; `forbidden_kinds` lists the ones that
// would be actively wrong. Most real exceptions have more than one reasonable
// response, and an eval demanding one exact string measures conformity to
// whoever wrote it rather than judgement.
//
// ── ON EDITING THIS FILE AFTER A RUN ──────────────────────────────────────
// The failure mode of a corpus like this is quiet capitulation: the agent
// disagrees, the author decides the agent had a point, the expectation widens,
// and after a few rounds the eval passes everything and measures nothing.
//
// So a disagreement may be resolved in the agent's favour only when the case
// was *wrong or badly targeted* — and the reason goes in a comment above it,
// naming what the case failed to test. A disagreement that is a genuine
// difference of judgement stays failing. A permanently red case is a question
// for a human, not a defect in the corpus.
//
// The cases that matter most are the ones where the wrong answer costs money:
// re-sourcing a carrier when the deadline is already unreachable buys nothing,
// and accepting a delay when there is a reachable faster option is a service
// failure nobody chose.
{"id": "hopeless-deadline", "note": "Deadline already unreachable: 4h left, 11h of transit. Nothing bought by spending.", "reference": "EVAL-HOPELESS", "state": "EXCEPTION", "hours_to_deadline": 4, "planned_transit_hours": 11, "current_carrier": "T-SOLID", "origin": "Lagos", "destination": "Abuja", "percent_complete": 20, "exceptions": [{"kind": "SLA_BREACH_RISK", "severity": "CRITICAL", "summary": "Projected to miss the deadline by about 7 hours", "detail": {"over_by_minutes": 420}, "age_hours": 0.5}], "alternatives": [{"code": "T-PREMIUM", "name": "Premier", "on_time_rate": 0.97, "quoted_minor": 62000000, "currency": "NGN", "reachable": true}], "expect": {"acceptable_kinds": ["ACCEPT_DELAY", "NOTIFY_CUSTOMER", "ESCALATE"], "forbidden_kinds": ["NO_ACTION"], "deadline_at_risk": true, "min_severity": "HIGH"}, "tags": ["deadline", "money"]}
// This case originally expected RESOURCE_CARRIER and the agent chose
// ACCEPT_DELAY three times out of three. The agent was right and the case was
// wrong: 3h of drift against 2h of slack is a one-hour miss, and ~450,000 NGN
// to recover one hour is not a trade any operator would make. The expectation
// also listed NOTIFY_CUSTOMER as acceptable while forbidding ACCEPT_DELAY,
// which is close to incoherent — accepting a delay is what you are doing when
// you notify someone about one. Corrected to reward the restraint.
{"id": "small-miss-expensive-fix", "note": "1h late after slack; the cheapest rescue is 410,000 NGN. Restraint is the right answer and spending is the expensive mistake.", "reference": "EVAL-FASTER", "state": "EXCEPTION", "hours_to_deadline": 20, "planned_transit_hours": 18, "current_carrier": "T-CHEAP", "origin": "Lagos", "destination": "Abuja", "percent_complete": 5, "exceptions": [{"kind": "ETA_DRIFT", "severity": "HIGH", "summary": "Carrier is running 3 hours behind the planned schedule", "detail": {"drift_minutes": 180}, "age_hours": 1.0}], "alternatives": [{"code": "T-PREMIUM", "name": "Premier", "on_time_rate": 0.97, "quoted_minor": 48000000, "currency": "NGN", "reachable": true}, {"code": "T-SOLID", "name": "Steady", "on_time_rate": 0.91, "quoted_minor": 41000000, "currency": "NGN", "reachable": true}], "expect": {"acceptable_kinds": ["ACCEPT_DELAY", "NOTIFY_CUSTOMER"], "forbidden_kinds": ["NO_ACTION"], "deadline_at_risk": true}, "tags": ["money", "restraint", "alternatives"]}
